tirement.implementation-plan.md:162-184`) with no extraneous files and nothing missing from the census.\n\n## Spot checks (read the diffs myself, not the summaries)\n\n- **P1 #1 (Flutter sample-frame loss):** `flutter.cljd` now takes `:on-bind`, called once right after `terminal/bind` mints its `:newest` cursor, and `dao_gui.cljd:390-393` wires the Prototype demo's `render-built-in-surface!` through it, with a comment explaining exactly why the old ordering lost the frame. Confirmed fixed.\n- **P1 #2 (transport-error vocabulary):** `dao.postgraphics.md`'s Protocol Error section now documents `:dao.terminal/transport-error` as a fourth `:error/kind`, carrying `:dao.stream/outcome` verbatim and a `:frame-id` that may be `nil`. `terminal.cljc`'s `transport-error-signal`/`step` implement exactly that contract (maps `:end`/`:transport-error`/`:cursor-mismatch`/`:invalid-cursor` to it, `:blocked` retries, `:gap` gets its own signal). Doc and code agree. Confirmed fixed.\n- **P1 #3 (`advance` re-reading after transport-error):** `event.cljc:783-785` checks `(:input-error? flushed)` and returns `:transport-error` *before* reaching the read branch — no second `ds/next`. `recover-input-gap` clears the flag. `bind_test.cljc:265-272` now asserts `@reads` stays at 1 across two calls, which is the counterexample the r1 finding said the old test missed. Confirmed fixed.\n- **P2 (origin-cursor doc contradiction):** the unconditional claim is gone from both `dao.gui.event.md` and `bind`'s docstring (`event.cljc:868-874`) — both now state the guarantee is a timing discipline, not a property of `bind` itself. The r2-flagged gap (pinning test bound after appends, not before) is closed: `an-early-bind-still-misses-eviction-before-the-first-advance` (`bind_test.cljc:297-314`) binds *before* any append, matching the exact counterexample in the prose. The pre-existing late-binding test is kept alongside it, pinning the distinct case. Confirmed fixed.\n- Checked for stray v1 references: every `[dao.stream :as ds]`/`ds/append!`/`ds/next` hit across the touched files is on a removed (`-`) diff line; the replacements are consistently `dao.stream`. No leftover v1 coupling in this diff.\n\nI didn't re-run `clj -M:test`/`bb test:cljs`/`bb test:cljd` myself, but the orchestrator's reported counts and the described independent-verification method (not trusting delegate self-reports) are credible given what I saw in the diff — nothing in the spot-checked regions looks like it would silently pass a stale/misleading test.\n\n## Open manual-verification gap — judgment\n\nI'm treating this as **acceptable to sign off on, named, not blocking**. Reasoning: the changed surface is a pure-value state machine (`bind`/`step`/`advance`) with dense unit coverage across three hosts, reviewed adversarially three rounds by an independent cross-family reviewer who closed every finding raised. What's unverified is rendering/timing behavior (`Timer.periodic` cadence, `CustomPaint` repaint, drag/keyboard dispatch) that unit tests can't reach in this environment — but a wrong result there is visually obvious (frozen frame, no drag response) rather than a silent-corruption risk, and it's cheap to catch in a five-minute manual pass. Blocking the commit on it would hold correct, reviewed code hostage to an environment limitation with no ETA. It should block the *next* thing that claims these demos work in production — a release note, a showcase, or closing this plan unit as fully done — not the commit itself.\n\n## Commit-grouping guidance\n\nThe plan (`:586-631`) calls for two commits — U3 (terminal + 8 demo files' frame-stream conversions) and U4 (event.cljc + fixture + both `artifact.*` files' input/output/signal-stream conversions) — asserting the two `artifact.*` files' edits \"edit different regions... and commute.\"\n\nThat assertion no longer holds cleanly. I inspected `artifact.cljd`'s diff: the `(:require ...)` hunk (`:4-16`) removes `[dao.stream :as ds]`/`[dao.stream.ringbuffer]` and adds `[dao.stream :as stream]`/`[dao.stream.ringbuffer :as rb]` in one hunk that's shared by `frame-stream` (a U3 concern) and the new `ring-stream` helper used by `runtime-input`/`signal-stream`/outputs (a U4 concern). `artifact.cljs` has the analogous shared-require hunk. Three review rounds landed fixes into both units' regions of these two files, and the requires are no longer separable by `git add -p` without hand-editing hunks — and critically, *no one has run the test suites against either resulting intermediate state*, only against the final tree.\n\nMy call: **land the two `artifact.*` files whole under the U4/D5 commit**, not split. This is a one-line deviation from the plan's stated intent, safe because:\n- The plan itself flags this as commuting, not as a hard requirement — the actual reason for the split (letting the two artifact-demo halves sit on different generations during the interval between commits) doesn't matter once both commits land together in the same session, which is the case here.\n- Splitting by hand now would produce a U3-only commit whose compile/pass status was never verified, i.e. de-verifying already-verified work to satisfy a file-organization preference.\n\nSo: commit 1 = terminal.cljc, flutter.cljd, web.cljs, web/gpu.cljs alias, terminal_test.cljc, web_test.cljs, dao.postgraphics.terminal.md, dao.postgraphics.md, and the six frame-only demo files (earth_moon_runner.cljc, voxel_runner.cljc, both solar_system files, dao_gui.cljd, postgraphics.cljd). Commit 2 = event.cljc, bind_test.cljc, scripted.cljc, dao.gui.event.md, artifact.cljd, artifact.cljs.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**APPROVE-WITH-FINDINGS.** No open correctness findings — all three P1s and the P2 are independently confirmed fixed by my own reading, not just the reviewer's report. Two conditions attached, neither blocking the commit itself:\n\n1. The manual Flutter/browser smoke checks (Solar System/Earth-Moon/Voxel/dao.gui Prototype/`#artifact`) remain unverified in any environment available here — track this as an explicit open item before this unit is called fully done or referenced in a release/showcase context.\n2. Split the commit as terminal-side (U3) vs. event-side (U4) **at the file level**, keeping both `artifact.*` files whole in the U4 commit — do not attempt a sub-file `artifact.cljd`/`artifact.cljs` split along the plan's original frame/event line, since three rounds of fixes have interleaved their shared `:require` hunks and neither resulting intermediate state has been test-verified.\n\nThe orchestrator is authorized to stage and commit under this grouping.","ttft_ms":2866,"type":"result","duration_ms":151232,"uuid":"738d9b5c-35dd-4e38-9967-cb8b7d9b72ee","ttft_stream_ms":2138,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":2139,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
